      "date": "2026-11-21 15:31:47.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(5 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nMostly good. I found no correctness problem in the chunked map/unmap logic, and there are a few comments inline. The chunked path also looks untested: test nodes without a translating IOMMU never chunk by default, so neither the map nor the unwind path runs in regular test sessions. Consider adding a sanity-lnet case that reloads ko2iblnd with a small dma_map_chunk_kb (e.g. 4 or 64) and runs bulk I/O, so kiblnd_dma_map_tx_frags() and kiblnd_dma_unmap_chunks() are exercised.",
