        "subject": "LU-21272 o2iblnd: map bulk DMA in IOVA-cacheable chunks",
        "message": "LU-21272 o2iblnd: map bulk DMA in IOVA-cacheable chunks\n\nBehind a translating IOMMU, every dma_map_sg() allocates one IOVA\nrange for the whole scatterlist. The IOMMU layer only caches ranges\nup to dma_opt_mapping_size() (128 KiB on current kernels) per CPU.\no2iblnd maps a whole LNet bulk (up to 1 MiB, 256 pages) in one call,\nso every bulk map and unmap goes to the rbtree allocator under the\nIOMMU domain's iova_rbtree_lock, first trying the 32-bit window. On\nRoCE clients with the IOMMU in translated mode, Lustre bulk throughput\ndrops to 1/2 or 1/3 of line rate on about a third of boots. With\niommu=pt, 0 of 21 boots degraded, versus 8 of 21 without it.\n\nMap tx_frags with one dma_map_sg() per chunk of at most\ndma_opt_mapping_size(), so each IOVA comes from the per-CPU cache.\nThe DMA segments of all chunks are packed into a new tx_dma_frags\narray, which feeds rd_frags and ib_map_mr_sg(). FastReg still\nregisters the whole bulk as one MR, so the wire protocol and the\nnumber of RDMAs are unchanged. Unmap splits the list the same way,\nusing only the page offsets and lengths that dma_map_sg() leaves\nintact.\n\nChunking follows dma_opt_mapping_size() of the device, not the IOMMU\nmode. With iommu=pt or no IOMMU, that size is usually larger than\na bulk, so the mapping does not change. A device that bounces through\nswiotlb reports about 256 KiB, and its bulks are chunked too. Kernels\nwithout dma_opt_mapping_size() do not chunk by default. Chunking is\noff when the IOMMU granule is smaller than PAGE_SIZE. The chunk IOVAs\nthen do not meet at page boundaries, and FastReg cannot register them\nas one MR. Bulks that already fit in one chunk, and P2P buffers, are\nstill mapped in a single call. The tx_dma_frags array\n(IBLND_MAX_RDMA_FRAGS entries per tx) is only allocated for pools\nthat chunk.\n\nAt device setup, print whether bulk DMA is mapped in chunks and the\nchunk size, and warn when the IOMMU translates the HCA's DMA\naddresses, so the setting shows up in the console log.\n\nAdd compat helpers for dma_get_merge_boundary(),\niommu_is_dma_domain() and dma_opt_mapping_size().\n\nAdd a ko2iblnd module parameter:\n  dma_map_chunk_kb=-1  use dma_opt_mapping_size() (default)\n  dma_map_chunk_kb=0   map each bulk in one call (old behaviour)\n  dma_map_chunk_kb=N   chunks of N KiB, e.g. on kernels without\n                       dma_opt_mapping_size()\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: nettype=o2ib testlist=sanity-lnet,sanity\nSigned-off-by: Ravindra Singh <rsingh@ddn.com>\nSigned-off-by: Cyril Bordage <cbordage@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nAssisted-by: Augment:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Ic8b71b3fde058394da777256c1603dfdc07545e9\n"
      },
